# FieldBourne Digital marketing site

`CLAUDE.md` in the repo root is the main instruction file: business context, writing rules, outreach compliance and guardrails. Read it first, then `BRANDING.md` (copy and voice), `PRODUCT.md` and `DESIGN.md` (design). If this file conflicts with `CLAUDE.md`, follow `CLAUDE.md`.

## Key files

- `src/config/site.ts`: form endpoint, phone, email, ABN, CRM app link, towns
- `src/index.css`: brand tokens in `@theme`
- `src/components/Ridgelines.tsx`: the Scenic Rim landscape and its scroll motion
- `src/pages/`: Home, Website review, Services, Pricing, Concept sites, Case study, Scenic Rim, About, legal
- `scripts/prerender.mjs`: saves every route as real HTML at build time; add new routes to `ROUTES` in `src/App.tsx`

## When editing

- Australian English. No em dashes. Nothing from the banned list in `BRANDING.md` section 5.
- Keep brand colours exact. Amber is for fills and marks, never small text.
- Use `site.ts` for contact details and URLs; don't hard-code them.
- One authored motion moment (the ridgelines). Always respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Never push to `main` without Darren's OK: it deploys the live site.
